YAFAP Siobhan-Wiz-Gno-Fem-Neu

Oh wow.

This has been a long time coming.  I started playing rouge on my old
mans 8088 in high school.  I have played while living in 4 US states,
Canada, The UK and ascended in Switzerland.

Siobhan was named for John Rebus' protege Siobhan Clarke in Ian
Rankins series of detective books, after I had killed Rebus, Farmer,
and many others.  Usually I manage to kill off my wizards much faster
than Valks and Barbs.  Mostly I play those three, I occasionally play
priests, samauri, monks or Archaeologists.

This is from memory, as I don't keep notes.

In this case the RNG was nice enough to give me alters on 3 of the
firt 5 levels (2 co-aligned) and Smokey potions were Gain Ability.
The only shops were 2 potion shops.  So I had some early wishes from
my thieving pets, SDSM, +2 helm of brilliance, Gauntlets of Dexterity,
and Eyes of the Overworld please.    Thanks.  Sacced for MagicBane.
Double bones file in the mines got me a bunch of spellbooks a magic
marker and 2 magic lamps. Speed boots got +0, t-shirt got +2.  My 2
large dos were slaughtering the peaceful mine inhabitants, so no big
problem.  Mine Town was also a bones with a magic marker and a magic
whistle and it was the one with the little shops so I was starting to
worry about my scroll supply.  Some price IDing  and  I started
reading scrolls from the bones files having blessed them.  "what class
would you like to Genocide?"  Master mind fl...  CLASS?

^H^H^H^H^H^H^H^H^H^H^H^H L. then ;.

Buffed up the armour a bit, took out MMF with a unblessed scroll, took
MB to +2 and the other daggers to +4.  Learned Charm monster at some
point, what a great spell.  Between that and a poly trap in the mines
my 2 pet dragons and pet MMF and I redistributed the wealth in
minetown from the shopkeepers to the priest, with Itzhak safley locked
away.  The Pet Mind Flayer was truely devastating, but eventually I
left him in Sokoban, which inever finished since I had a BoH and
reflection.

At this point I am pretty buffed up, ac ~-20, HP 100+, PW 150+, and
unlimited E-word.  Not to mention the Magic whistle for my little
friends.  So I cleaned out up to Medusa without much problem including
fort ludios, which i did without pets so that I could finish off my
resistances I was wearing a amulet of poison resist up to this point.

Once I saw the titan (who killed my previous best effort with a
summoning storm and a big assist from my own stupidity) I went back up
and found the quest.  The only issue, and the closest I came to dying
in this whole game was when I hit the Dark one with the potion of
paralysis I was not wearing either of my rings of free action.  Stupid
but not fatal, woke up, hit the whistle, then tickled him to death
with MB.  Free action stayed on one finger for most of the rest of the
game.  Set the prisoners free, unfortunately they did not get along
with Mr. Jabberwok.

Went back to Medusa, gave the Titan the Finger, dug down, came up
blindfolded, bye bye medusa, got the levitation boots from perseus.

Now this is officially my best game ever.

Didn't bother with the guillotine, just hit it with a wand of
striking, then between conflict and the finger it was no big deal.
Wished up some magic markers and finished off my Armour and did some
genoing, and polypiling, didn't get much interesting except my first
Amulet of lifesaving.  Did some alchemy to get the HP up. Sorted the
stash at the Castle and went down. Genoed T since they were pissing me
off.

Waded though the valley, and unfortunately didn't do any wraith
luring.  Then Ghenomon.  What a disappointment.  Now I understand why
people get bored here.  Paid off Bezelbub and someone else.  Wandered
through Orcus town so I had to recharge his wand of death.  Jubilex
was a little exciting, but the Unihorn and wand of digging make quick
work of him.  Any time one of my Minotaurs wanderd onto a Polytrap and
turned into a ant or something equally useless I charmed another one.
There were not many slimes, but MM and fireball sorted tham out pretty
well.

One of the Minotaur minions took out Vlad while I was clearing the
other rooms, so that was easy, i didn't know they could open doors.

Finding the Vibrating square was a pain.  I love the Eyes of the
Overworld, but they make it hard to tell where you have been already
in the mazes,  I wound up digging the whole bottom level in stripes.

I got some doubts in my mind since G was so easy I posted to RGRN to
make sure I wasn't forgetting anything.

 Then life intervened.  I had to put the game down for the weekend and
work was crazy when I came back, so it sat for several days.  Although
I had several nethack dreams.

Came back last weekend. Gave Rodney the finger grabbed the book and
ran.  Ditched all the pets. Did the invocation. Went down, and back
up.  Read

cursed Tele to go back down, as suggested here.  It took me down
within sight of the stairs, great /sarcasam.  Waded through the masses
Charmed some new pets, gave the finger liberally.  The Eye of the A is
definitely a must have for spell casters. got the Amulet and quaffed
Cursed gain level.

The mysterious force was a real pain in the ass.  It especially liked
sending me back to no teleport levels.  I had to do Jubilex at least 4
times. It also liked to send me as far away from explored or dug
levels as possible.  But through all that Rodney only showed up twice.
Finger, bye.

At the castle I grabbed all my digging and tele wands, crap artifacts
from Saccing and gems. and the force calmed down considerably, or
maybe being out of the mazes and no tele levels just made it not as
bothersome.  Rodney one more time in the big room. Grabbed the stash
on LVL1 killed a fox who must have been there for a long time (for my
lowest single) and went up.

Had way more wands of digging than I needed for earth.  Charmed messes
of elementals and conflict took care of the rest I guess Rodney showed
up here as well, finger. Put on levetation and went to...

Air Was by far the hardest Hung out in Vortexes to recover power a
couple of times, but the Air elementals are FAST.  Charmed some of
them, but Power was in short supply after I accidentally charmed the
vortexes, had to quaff a couple of FH.  Teleport and running were the
only answer.

Fire, Something was summoning, so I charmed some more and since I was
still levitating went over the lava.  Whistle, Water.  Took a while to
get to the portal, I guess I could have used magical breathing to get
through the water, but the pet fire elementals were beating the water
elementals pretty well, so eventually i took off conflict and went to

Astral!  Oh boy did my heart rate go up here.  The light, walk towards
the light!  I went left.  Wand of death to Famine.  I thought you
could Teleport the corpse.  Nope. Wand of death again.  Teleported a
path and Jumped in.  Lawful.  Shit.  Jumped out.  Killed Famine
again.  Put on Conflict, pissed off my angel, oops.  Ran to the
center, WoD to Pesty.  Same drill, Tele, jump, Chaotic.  SHIT.

This seemed to be a good time to save, have a smoke and see what the
spoilers have to say about killing death (who scares me to himself).
Not much,  hmm, I guess I will have a look.  The first room looks like
this:
